WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:05.320
The One Piece manga just added a SHOCKING TWIST&nbsp;
to Kuma's backstory which has left me desperately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:11.840
rereading every single panel of Kuma, Bonney, and&nbsp;
Luffy’s interactions to see if maybe, just maybe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:18.480
there’s a chance that Luffy and Bonney are&nbsp;
actually related. And all this comes because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:26.200
at the end of this chapter Kuma mysteriously&nbsp;
arrives at Foosha village, which is where Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:34.720
was born and raised. Now, what is he doing here?&nbsp;
We aren’t shown quite yet, but since the backstory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:40.120
is not yet over I imagine we will be finding out&nbsp;
very soon. However, that isn’t going to stop us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:45.480
from speculating what this all means and how it&nbsp;
completely changes what we thought we knew about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:51.400
Kuma and Luffy. And to start, let’s go through&nbsp;
the possibilities for why Kuma might have come to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:58.440
Foosha village. Now keep in mind that this is all&nbsp;
after Kuma has been turned into a cyborg and has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:05.460
had his memories somewhat altered. However we do&nbsp;
know that he didn’t have his memories completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:13.400
erased until the time skip, so at this point,&nbsp;
he likely still remembered most of who he was.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:19.160
Now the most obvious reason that he would be&nbsp;
coming here would be because of course Monkey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:23.760
D. Dragon, who is the Revolutionary&nbsp;
Army commander and Kuma’s friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.960
was also most likely born and raised here. So&nbsp;
it is entirely possible that Kuma was coming to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.440
meet Dragon and talk to him about his plans now&nbsp;
that he was a cyborg. And of course, you might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:41.920
saying there is no way that Kuma would do this&nbsp;
since he is now partially a government slave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:47.160
but remember that Warlords are basically free&nbsp;
to do whatever they want unless they are given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:52.600
a direct order by the world government, which&nbsp;
as we’ve seen doesn’t happen all that often.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:58.240
On top of that, Kuma has shown us many times in&nbsp;
the pre-time skip that he would follow his own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:03.360
will instead of just blindly following the world&nbsp;
government’s commands. In fact, during Sabaody,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:09.800
he even tells Rayleigh that he is still an officer&nbsp;
of the Revolutionary Army. So all that to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:15.200
it is completely possible that Kuma is still&nbsp;
acting as a revolutionary at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.320
which makes it possible that&nbsp;
he would go meet with Dragon.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:23.800
Now, why would he do that? Well, the most&nbsp;
logical reason is that Dragon asked Kuma&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:28.800
to watch over Luffy. Which just makes a lot&nbsp;
of sense because of Kuma’s actions later on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:34.960
in Thriller Bark and Sabaody. For example, after&nbsp;
the Straw Hats defeated the Warlord Gecko Moria,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:42.720
Kuma was tasked with wiping out everyone on the&nbsp;
entire island, including Luffy and the straw hats.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:48.400
And I know I’m trying to convince you that Kuma&nbsp;
is an ally here, but man for a few chapters it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:55.560
certainly looked like Kuma was going to kill them&nbsp;
all pretty easily. Now it is debatable how much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:01.160
free will he had here and how much of that was&nbsp;
his forced government programming, but eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:08.360
he let the straw hats escape after Zoro’s display&nbsp;
of loyalty. But then in chapter 485 as Kuma was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:15.360
leaving the island, he revealed that he already&nbsp;
knew that Luffy was Dragon’s son. So clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:20.880
he must have learned about Luffy and Dragon’s&nbsp;
relationship at some point in the recent past.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.880
And while you might think that it would be simple&nbsp;
to connect Luffy to his father because of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:34.080
shared family name, not many characters were able&nbsp;
to do that. And even some of Dragon’s most trusted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:41.280
allies in the Revolutionaries, such as this guy&nbsp;
didn’t even know that Dragon had a son. So clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:47.400
this wasn’t common knowledge, which means that&nbsp;
Kuma must have learned in some unique situation.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:52.760
Which makes Kuma’s surprise visit to the Goa&nbsp;
kingdom at the end of this chapter the perfect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:59.360
opportunity for Dragon to reveal that he has a son&nbsp;
and ask Kuma to watch over him as best he can from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.600
within the World Government. Which is just amazing&nbsp;
if that was somehow planned from the very start...

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.600
…and honestly, that just goes to show, that&nbsp;
this entire arc so far has had some of the best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:16.160
character writing ever in one piece, and as you&nbsp;
know that really says something. May I remind you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:22.160
that we just had a giant blue alcoholic dragon as&nbsp;
the last big villain, who I still think was super&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:27.720
underrated as a character, building his empire in&nbsp;
Wano. And if you ever felt like you also want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:33.560
have your very own personal dragon empire, worry&nbsp;
not because today’s sponsor allows you to do just&nbsp;&nbsp;

