00:05:23.511 --> 00:05:29.840
However, some parts of the story go against the&nbsp;
idea that Dragon asked Kuma to watch over Luffy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:35.040
For example, Kuma’s visit to Foosha village must&nbsp;
have happened sometime around three or so years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:43.520
before the current story. This would have been&nbsp;
just after Kuma had become a warlord. At this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:49.560
point, Luffy was still at Foosha village, but&nbsp;
Ace had already left to become a pirate and had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:54.080
already defeated a Warlord himself. However,&nbsp;
that just makes me wonder how would Dragon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:59.560
keep tabs on Luffy but then not know that&nbsp;
he was going to become a pirate, since it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:09.760
seem that was new information to him in chapter&nbsp;
100. I mean this was Luffy’s dream all along,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:16.360
and I’m pretty sure everyone in Foosha village&nbsp;
knew he wanted to be a pirate the whole time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:22.160
Luffy was growing up. So sure, you could say that&nbsp;
Dragon is not the greatest father and even if he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:26.960
was watching Luffy he might not have figured out&nbsp;
what he wanted to be, but for now let’s assume&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:32.960
that this isn’t actually the case and that Dragon&nbsp;
did not invite Kuma to Foosha village after all.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:38.520
Then what other reason could Kuma&nbsp;
have for coming to the kingdom? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:45.440
there are a few other reasons that I can&nbsp;
think of and one of them is absolutely going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:50.800
to blow your mind with its possibilities. But&nbsp;
first, it is possible Kuma went there for some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:55.640
unknown reason that we will find out in the next&nbsp;
chapter or so. It could have just been random,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:58.280
though it doesn't seem to have been&nbsp;
ordered by the world government.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:04.360
It is also possible that Kuma went to Foosha&nbsp;
village because this was the island that he and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:12.000
Ginny were supposed to meet up on before Ginny was&nbsp;
captured. We learned about this in chapter 1097,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:19.080
so maybe Kuma went there for nostalgia or just&nbsp;
to remember something about his past love.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:24.560
BUT ANOTHER POSSIBILITY... Ohh boy, we’re&nbsp;
going to have fun with this one. This one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:29.480
also involves Ginny, but gets WAY MORE&nbsp;
INTERESTING. To start, let’s make sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:36.200
we all understand a few details. First, Ginny was&nbsp;
the Revolutionary Army’s Eastern Forces Commander,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:42.840
so it is entirely possible that Ginny already&nbsp;
had visited Foosha village or the larger island,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:48.720
Dawn Island, sometime during her time with&nbsp;
the Revolutionaries. And in case you forgot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:56.000
Ginny was part of the Revolutionaries from about&nbsp;
22 years ago until she was captured about 14 years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:03.520
ago. Which means she was probably in the East&nbsp;
Blue for quite some time. Now the point I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:09.600
trying to make takes us way back to some of the&nbsp;
initial speculation surrounding Ginny when she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:16.880
was first introduced in chapter 1095. And that&nbsp;
of course is that Ginny might actually be Luffy's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:22.880
mother after all. I mean, she was most likely&nbsp;
in the East Blue around the time Luffy was born,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:28.640
which was nineteen years ago. She has close&nbsp;
ties with Dragon, as well as all the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:33.320
reasons she might be Luffy's mother that we&nbsp;
had discussed in prior chapter reviews such as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:38.240
the similarities with eating lots of food and&nbsp;
the similar names. At the time we had thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:45.400
she might be Luffy OR Bonney’s mom, but what&nbsp;
if she was both of their mothers all along?

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.240
Now you might be angrily typing away&nbsp;
in the comments right now that there’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:51.640
no way she would betray her love for&nbsp;
Kuma like that, but I’m just saying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:57.600
it’s possible. Even if that is not the case&nbsp;
though, I wonder if she could have met Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:02.760
at one point and she was inspired by his&nbsp;
personality, just like Shanks was. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:07.760
Luffy wouldn’t have had his straw hat or&nbsp;
devil fruit when Ginny was around because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:14.880
he didn’t get either of those things until at&nbsp;
least a year after she was captured. Still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:21.440
Luffy is pretty hard to forget as a kid, so even&nbsp;
if she isn’t his mother, maybe Ginny figured out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:28.680
that he was Dragon’s son and mentioned it to Kuma,&nbsp;
which led Kuma here as we see in the flashback.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:34.480
But now that I’m thinking about it, I wonder if&nbsp;
there is another possibility for why Kuma came to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:41.000
Luffy’s home island. Because remember that Kuma&nbsp;
is part of the Buccaneer race who are known for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:47.720
believing in Nika. We also know that Nika is&nbsp;
commonly referred to as the Sun God and Kuma’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:53.400
father believed that Nika would bring freedom&nbsp;
to the world. Well, one thing that we know is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.400 --> 00:10:00.720
that all throughout One Piece is that the Dawn, or&nbsp;
the rising sun, is often used to symbolize freedom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:06.680
in the story. So what if part of the Nika lore&nbsp;
that Kuma knows also relates to Luffy’s home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:13.560
which again is on Dawn Island, as being part&nbsp;
of some special prophecy or something? This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:18.720
could also be part of the reason he went against&nbsp;
the government on Sabaody and made Vegapunk make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:25.560
it his mission to protect the Sunny for two years&nbsp;
because he had some idea that Luffy might be Nika.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:33.800
Or another possibility is that Kuma came here&nbsp;
with a completely different purpose. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:41.240
one of the special things about Kuma's devil fruit&nbsp;
is that it can do some pretty incredible things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:46.840
like push out memories for example. So what&nbsp;
if he actually came to do something similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:53.120
to Luffy? I mean we all know Luffy didn’t even&nbsp;
know who his father was until his grandpa told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:58.360
him in chapter 432, and we all just assumed&nbsp;
that Luffy was just being an idiot like usual.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:03.960
But what if instead Kuma somehow pushed&nbsp;
out Luffy’s memories of his parents for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:09.560
some unknown reason? I know it sounds a bit&nbsp;
sketchy for Kuma to do something like that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:13.840
plus that means Luffy might have known about&nbsp;
his parents during most of his childhood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:19.920
but still, I think this idea of Kuma taking&nbsp;
something from Luffy could come back around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:25.080
in the future, especially if Kuma had a&nbsp;
hint that Luffy might actually be Nika.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:30.200
Which sounds crazy, I know, but I’m just throwing&nbsp;
it out there. But if there's one thing that has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:35.680
been most surprising about Kuma’s flashback&nbsp;
is how he literally has connections to so many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:40.160
characters and places all around the world.&nbsp;
I mean last chapter we saw how he visited all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:44.400
the places he sent the Straw Hats during the&nbsp;
timeskip, so at this point I want to make one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:48.920
more connection in regards to Bonney. Listen&nbsp;
to this. One thing I just haven’t been able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:56.360
figure out this entire flashback is how this&nbsp;
backstory ties into Bonney’s future. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.360 --> 00:12:03.160
one thing that flashbacks in one piece always do&nbsp;
is clarify a character’s motivations and dreams.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:08.040
We saw it with Chopper’s inspiration to become a&nbsp;
doctor, Robin’s dedication to become a scholar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:13.960
and even Law’s desire for vengeance against&nbsp;
Doflamingo. And if we take it even further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:18.960
extensive flashbacks like this are usually&nbsp;
saved for future straw hats or characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:24.120
that will be important allies for the Straw Hats&nbsp;
in the future. Take Vivi’s flashback for example&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:29.360
or the Wano flashback which showed Momo’s birth&nbsp;
and upbringing. However, both of those characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:35.280
are leaders of important countries who will&nbsp;
no doubt come to Luffy’s aid in the future.

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:40.920
But Bonney certainly isn’t the leader of a&nbsp;
super strong country. Unless she is secretly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:46.520
the new queen of Sorbet kingdom, I guess. But&nbsp;
assuming Sorbet isn't some super military power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:52.360
that leaves the main reason for her being&nbsp;
involved in a flashback like this is that she is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:58.840
a potential straw hat candidate. And the more you&nbsp;
look into the more she fits a lot of the criteria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:04.640
that are required for characters to join the crew.&nbsp;
First, she obviously has a tragic backstory. Next,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:08.600
if she wants to fulfill Kuma’s dreams of&nbsp;
helping Nika bring freedom to the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:14.960
that is a clear dream that she can fulfill while&nbsp;
traveling with Luffy. As for her role on the crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:17.840
well if we take the fact that&nbsp;
she is only twelve years old,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:21.120
then she could certainly fill the&nbsp;
role of cabin girl or apprentice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:25.360
much like Shanks and Buggy were on Roger’s&nbsp;
crew. Although that might be a bit of a stretch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:31.800
considering she’s already been a pretty famous&nbsp;
captain on her own when she aged herself up.

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:37.880
However, this idea of Bonney making herself&nbsp;
seem older than she is also relates to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:43.560
next part of why she could be such a perfect&nbsp;
straw hat candidate. Because one other thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:50.000
that every potential straw hat must have is that&nbsp;
they need Luffy to free them somehow. For Nami,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:54.120
it was literally freeing her from Arlong. For&nbsp;
Robin, it was giving her the confidence to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.120 --> 00:14:00.680
know that she deserved to live. For Sanji, it was&nbsp;
helping him understand that it was okay for him to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:06.840
follow his dreams. Well, for Bonney she also has&nbsp;
something that she needs to learn. Which is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:12.120
she doesn’t have to pretend to be an adult when&nbsp;
she is still just a kid. I mean for as long as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:17.160
we’ve known her she has been pushing herself to be&nbsp;
an adult with her devil fruit powers. She’s been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:22.200
doing this all this time as she fights to find&nbsp;
Kuma and free him from the world government. Yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:28.080
all this time she has refused to believe that&nbsp;
Kuma sacrificed himself for her. It’s honestly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:34.440
super tragic that she refuses to believe that&nbsp;
Kuma would choose to become a mindless slave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:39.320
as we see during this conversation with Akainu&nbsp;
during the timeskip. So the way that Luffy can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:44.880
help her is to gain closure from the fact that&nbsp;
Kuma sacrificed himself so that she can have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:50.800
normal life. She doesn’t need to pretend to be an&nbsp;
adult and that she can just be herself. It’s kinda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:57.040
similar to Chopper, who believed himself to be a&nbsp;
monster until the crew accepted him as who he was.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:02.000
So again, there’s a lot of potential here&nbsp;
for Bonney to join the crew after this arc.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:06.480
Then again, it is possible she might not. In&nbsp;
fact, Bonney already seems to have made some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:11.120
peace with her father’s memories as we saw&nbsp;
in chapter 1090. In this scene right here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:15.160
Luffy points out that Bonney is acting&nbsp;
much happier than before and she says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:18.320
that she feels much better than the&nbsp;
day before when she first saw her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:23.680
father’s memories. So maybe she is already&nbsp;
starting to accept what Kuma did for her.

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:28.120
Now, we’ve spent this entire review so far talking&nbsp;
about the plot twist at the end, so let’s touch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:33.000
on the other parts of the chapter. So much like&nbsp;
we expected, Saturn interfered with Vegapunk’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:37.920
planned operation and added the condition that&nbsp;
Kuma must have his memories erased by the end of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:45.680
the procedure. Which man, every arc Oda makes us&nbsp;
hate a new character even more than the last one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:52.360
and Saturn is definitely living up to the new&nbsp;
biggest scumbag in the story. Strangely enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:56.680
though, Kuma’s full cyborg transformation&nbsp;
will take two full years to complete,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.680 --> 00:16:03.240
so I guess they are doing it in stages. But either&nbsp;
way, Kuma happily accepts this arrangement if it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:07.800
means that Bonney will be cured. Also, we&nbsp;
learned that Bonney’s treatment to cure her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:14.040
disease will take six months plus another year&nbsp;
of staying out of the sun to 100% recover. Which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:19.480
is how we get this awesome family bonding time&nbsp;
during this chapter of Kuma, Bonney, Vegapunk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.480 --> 00:16:25.640
Sentomaru, and even Kizaru enjoying themselves&nbsp;
on Egghead island in between surgeries. Which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:31.640
again just further reminds us that Kizaru&nbsp;
really was friends with all of these people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:36.640
so he might still have a change of heart&nbsp;
and decide to help his former friends.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:43.440
Once this time is over though, Bonney is taken&nbsp;
back to Sorbet kingdom where she lives inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:47.880
the church under the watch of a medical team,&nbsp;
who are really Cipher Pol agents who are there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:51.760
to keep track of her. All of this is so that&nbsp;
Kuma is forced to follow through with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:57.600
procedures to have his memories erased, and&nbsp;
Bonney will only be fully free once Kuma is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:03.760
fully a government slave. Which might actually&nbsp;
finally explain this conversation with Akainu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:09.960
in chapter 595 where the former admiral was&nbsp;
legit worried that Bonney had escaped. To me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:15.040
this means that Bonney ran away from Cipher Pol&nbsp;
before Kuma’s memories were erased, meaning that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:20.360
Kuma could have left the world government without&nbsp;
actually following through with the procedure. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:20.360 --> 00:17:25.680
I wonder if Bonney's condition will show up again&nbsp;
since she might not have completed the full year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:32.400
of recovery. Her leaving early also brings up the&nbsp;
question of why Kuma didn't leave the government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:37.560
once she escaped. Did he just not know that Bonney&nbsp;
had escaped? Or was he worried that the government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:42.720
would just capture her again if he rebelled? Or&nbsp;
did he have another reason for staying with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:47.280
government? Maybe he had some other mission he&nbsp;
wanted to fulfill for the Revolutionaries or he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:52.240
actually was looking out for Luffy all along. It&nbsp;
is almost certain that Luffy and the crew would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:58.040
have been wiped out at Sabaody if it weren’t for&nbsp;
Kuma. Plus he defended their ship for two years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:02.680
so all that is just more evidence that he&nbsp;
was doing all he could to make sure Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:07.720
had every chance to reach his potential.&nbsp;
We’re not sure at this point, but one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:13.200
thing is certain and that is this backstory&nbsp;
just continues to get more and more tragic.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:19.200
I mean Kuma writing a letter to the daughter he&nbsp;
will never see again… Kuma with the heartbreaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:24.800
last words, “Thank you for being born”. Bonney&nbsp;
laughing even because she thinks they can go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:30.960
back to being a family. Just come on. I know&nbsp;
some people are ready to end the backstory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:38.360
and get back to the action on Egghead, but&nbsp;
this is peak Oda backstory writing and I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:43.040
really can’t get enough of it. And honestly, I&nbsp;
might even rank this backstory right up in my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:46.840
top three backstories in the entire story,&nbsp;
but if you want to decide for yourself by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:52.520
comparing it to every other backstory in one&nbsp;
piece, you can watch this video right here.

00:18:57.520 --> 00:19:00.840
Shanks for watching and I’ll&nbsp;
see you in the next one.

